1H  10. Cirrus clouds are high, wispy clouds composed of ice crystals.\e[11;1H  11. Cirrostratus clouds can produce halos around the Sun or Moon.\e[12;1H  12. Cirrocumulus clouds often appear as rows of small white ripples.\e[13;1H  13. Altocumulus clouds often form patches of rounded cloud elements at middle levels.\e[14;1H  14. Altostratus clouds can make the Sun look like a blurred disk.\e[15;1H  15. Nimbostratus clouds commonly bring widespread, steady rain or snow.\e[16;1H  16. Cumulonimbus clouds can produce lightning, hail, and heavy rain.\e[17;1H  17. A mature thunderstorm can develop an anvil-shaped top as its updraft spreads outward.\e[18;1H  18. Lenticular clouds often form in atmospheric waves downwind of mountains.\e[19;1H  19. Mammatus clouds have pouchlike features that hang beneath a cloud base.\e[20;3H20. A\e[20;9Hshelf\e[20;15Hcloud\e[20;21Hcan\e[20;25Hform\e[20;30Halong\e[20;36Hthe\e[20;40Hleading\e[20;48Hedge\e[20;53Hof\e[20;56Ha\e[20;58Hthunderstorm’s\e[20;73Houtflow.\e[21;3H21. Virga\e[21;13Hconsists\e[21;22Ho
